# The commit-msg hook is a POSIX shell script: a CRLF shebang is not executable, and
# core.autocrlf=true would hand every checkout CRLF line endings. Scoped to .githooks/ so no
# existing file's checkout changes.
.githooks/** text eol=lf

# The role seed is a byte-for-byte copy of a charter a reader wrote, and its sha256 is quoted in the commit
# that added it: a CRLF checkout would change those bytes and quietly make that claim false. `-text` keeps
# both the blob and every checkout as the reader's own file, and it is scoped to this folder so no existing
# file's checkout changes.
data/roles/** -text
